[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The desk's own code says
otherwise. Run over the same reports, it finds more than one problem, and the parser fix covers
only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket. Shipping the parser fix closes the first
row only.
</Callout>

## The problems

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **parser**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get day and
  month swapped: 7 April lands on 4 July. App, email, and the booking-v2 form.
- **hint**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month
  first, the form reads the tenant's way. A bug in the form, not the parser.
- **one-day shift**: these dates move by one day, they are not swapped ("Lisbon got Tuesday,
  Toronto got Monday"). A time-zone bug. The desk listed them in `desk-notes.json` but filed
  them under parser by tenant.

## What the desk table shows

The incident page's own table, unchanged. Its footnote is the one-day shift, counted inside parser.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Why it was merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone, so nobody
reads the body. Subjects here say "wrong day" for all three problems. Intake's tag comes from the
reporter's browser, not the tenant, and it disagrees with the tenant's cause on many reports.
Place a report by tenant, channel and body, as `causes.ts` already does.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
